    ["s0052","idiomatic","Edict text was on a tablet one foot two inches long, four inches wide, eight lines thick; the empress's family reply tablet matched.","Edict text was on a tablet one foot two inches long, four inches wide, and eight fen thick; the empress's family reply tablet matched.","厚八分 gives tablet thickness as eight fen (分 as a linear measure), not lines; the replacement restores that measure and keeps the rest faithful.","high","applied"],
    ["s0052","literal","The edict text was on a tablet one foot two inches long, four inches wide, and eight lines thick; the empress's family reply tablet was the same.","The edict text was on a tablet one foot two inches long, four inches wide, and eight fen thick; the empress's family reply tablet was the same.","Same measure error in the literal field: 厚八分 is eight fen thick, not eight lines thick.","high","applied"],
    ["s0058","idiomatic","The host said: \"My son is unworthy; honored by the imperial inquiry, I dare not refuse.\"","The host said: \"My daughter is unworthy; honored by the imperial inquiry, I dare not refuse.\"","In this 問名 reply after 奉制問名, 臣某之子 names the bridal daughter; rendering 子 as \"son\" mis-sexes the referent in the marriage rite.","high","applied"],
    ["s0058","literal","The host said: \"My son So-and-so is unworthy; having received the imperial inquiry, I So-and-so dare not decline.\"","The host said: \"My daughter So-and-so is unworthy; having received the imperial inquiry, I So-and-so dare not decline.\"","Literal field has the same bridal-context error: 子 here is the daughter under name-inquiry, not a son.","high","applied"],
    ["s0077","idiomatic","The envoy firmly declined.\"","The envoy said: \"I firmly venture to decline.\"","使者曰：「某敢固辭。」 is direct speech; the idiomatic line is truncated and ends with a stray quote, and the proposed wording restores the speech form.","high","applied"],
    ["s0079","idiomatic","The envoy said he must finally decline.\"","The envoy said: \"I dare finally decline.\"","使者曰：「敢終辭。」 is direct speech; the idiomatic paraphrase plus stray closing quote should be restored to quoted first-person decline.","high","applied"],
    ["s0111","idiomatic","The envoy stood east outside the main gate, east-facing.","The envoy stood west outside the main gate, east-facing.","大門外之西，東面立 places the envoy west outside the great gate facing east; \"east outside\" reverses 西.","high","applied"],
    ["s0111","literal","The envoy stood east of the outer great gate, east-facing.","The envoy stood west of the outer great gate, east-facing.","Literal field likewise misreads 大門外之西 as east of the gate; west with east-facing stance matches the Chinese.","high","applied"],
    ["s0254","idiomatic","The Chief Palace Lady knelt north-facing and reported: \"The rite is complete,\" and rose.\"","The Chief Palace Lady knelt north-facing and reported: \"The rite is complete,\" and rose.","The trailing quote after \"rose\" is stray English corruption; removing it leaves an otherwise accurate rendering of 奏稱：「禮畢，興。」","high","applied"],
    ["s0254","literal","The Chief Palace Lady knelt north-facing and reported: \"The rite is complete,\" and rose.\"","The Chief Palace Lady knelt north-facing and reported: \"The rite is complete,\" and rose.","Literal field has the same stray closing quote after \"rose\"; deleting it corrects the corruption without changing sense.","high","applied"]
  ],
